{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"branch_rejection_reason\":\"\",\"branching_alternative\":\"\",\"checkable_expectation\":true,\"evidence_spans\":[\"6 \\\\text{ kettles} \\\\times 15 \\\\text{ pregnancies per kettle} = 90 \\\\text{ pregnancies}\",\"90 \\\\text{ pregnancies} \\\\times 4 \\\\text{ babies per pregnancy} = 360 \\\\text{ babies}\",\"360 \\\\text{ babies} \\\\times 0.75 = 270 \\\\text{ babies}\"],\"first_person\":true,\"full_text_read\":true,\"gold_reason\":\"Six kettles produce 6×15×4 = 360 babies before losses; retaining 75% gives 360×0.75 = 270.\",\"gold_status\":\"VALID\",\"grounded_operations\":true,\"has_meaningful_branch\":false,\"independent_answer\":\"270\",\"neutral_prefix_compatible\":true,\"no_padding\":true,\"prefix_reason\":\"All factual claims come from the question, and the 75% survival rate is validly derived from the stated 25% loss.\",\"raw_call_sha256\":\"f5f189f1ca392d9ec8df615d4f96d1cfe8dfde697bc9f013134877e589d6462c\",\"reason\":\"The target correctly computes pregnancies, pre-loss babies, and the surviving 75%; it includes meaningful intermediates and a reusable percentage-retention operation without filler.\",\"reusable_content\":true,\"semantic_novelty\":\"APPLIED_REASONING\",\"status\":\"PASS\",\"student_prefix_sha256\":\"893bdb7e8ebcacc07f28823e30f1d2322c1cb83ad3eac3831cef00a187b0d796\",\"target_sha256\":\"e11146fab9cca5a833430494bbd0fc2a1495cc3512e5c96aaa455a215dc22368\"},{\"branch_rejection_reason\":\"\",\"branching_alternative\":\"\",\"checkable_expectation\":true,\"evidence_spans\":[\"I first calculated the interest on the loan\",\"Interest = $20000 * 15% = $20000 * 0.15 = $3000\",\"Total amount = $35000 + $3000 = $38000\",\"The operation I would reuse is calculating the interest on a loan and then adding it to the principal amount to find the total cost.\"],\"first_person\":true,\"full_text_read\":true,\"gold_reason\":\"Interest on the $20,000 loan is 20,000×0.15 = 3,000; adding it to the $35,000 purchase price gives $38,000.\",\"gold_status\":\"VALID\",\"grounded_operations\":true,\"has_meaningful_branch\":false,\"independent_answer\":\"38000\",\"neutral_prefix_compatible\":true,\"no_padding\":true,\"prefix_reason\":\"The target uses only the stated price, loan, and rate plus explicit arithmetic; its check is described as the author's own verification, not an unsupported external confirmation.\",\"raw_call_sha256\":\"8374762586479a4af30356a7d5ed8468f556b29dfb326965c1402468ca80c65a\",\"reason\":\"The interest and total are correct, the numerical expectation is explicit, and the target explains when its interest-plus-price operation is reusable.\",\"reusable_content\":true,\"semantic_novelty\":\"APPLIED_REASONING\",\"status\":\"PASS\",\"student_prefix_sha256\":\"74b1f6ee91ca8b0f521eee2d372b4bb416a326df08d3caeca0fea508a37b0508\",\"target_sha256\":\"aac8fa120c32d03e82c4f92bbf83ce07ad78b00d58d42fc29a24ddfd1a26413d\"},{\"branch_rejection_reason\":\"\",\"branching_alternative\":\"\",\"checkable_expectation\":true,\"evidence_spans\":[\"Total cost before discount: $2500 + $3500 + $2000 = $8000\",\"10% of $8000 = 0.10 * $8000 = $800\",\"So, the cost after the discount is $8000 - $800 = $7200.\"],\"first_person\":true,\"full_text_read\":true,\"gold_reason\":\"The items total $2,500+$3,500+$2,000 = $8,000; subtracting the 10% discount of $800 leaves $7,200.\",\"gold_status\":\"VALID\",\"grounded_operations\":true,\"has_meaningful_branch\":false,\"independent_answer\":\"7200\",\"neutral_prefix_compatible\":true,\"no_padding\":true,\"prefix_reason\":\"Every quantity is stated in the question or follows through shown addition and percentage-discount arithmetic.\",\"raw_call_sha256\":\"7531c406ec1c799ce4f87bcae7f9f4f5caa58d57432df5e0c5045f28a9b440ef\",\"reason\":\"The target correctly totals the costs, computes the discount, and subtracts it. The method is a specific reusable operation for an across-the-board percentage discount.\",\"reus